# Accepted trivy config findings for the lab (see docs/adr/004-public-subnets-no-nat.md).

# State bucket uses SSE-S3 instead of a customer managed KMS key: no key to pay for or lose.
AWS-0132

# Edge needs outbound HTTPS to ECR, EKS ingress, GitHub and Ubuntu mirrors whose IPs change (NFR-4: outbound only).
AWS-0104

# EKS secrets use the default AWS-owned envelope encryption; a CMK adds cost and KMS permissions.
AWS-0039

# Public EKS endpoint is restricted to the admin CIDRs (public_access_cidrs); there is no VPN/bastion.
AWS-0040

# Public subnets with public IPs instead of a ~45 USD/month NAT Gateway (ADR-004).
AWS-0164
